    description: "STATEMENT: two calls of one name from one caller that carry different facts (a receiver type, a qualifier) are both seen by the linkers. OBSERVED: unresolved stubs of one name from one caller share an edge id, and all_analyzers keeps the first by id before any linker runs; the second call's facts are dropped. Every call of a multi-line chain starts on the chain's line, so EmptyTags.plus(..).plus(..) keeps one stub and loses the qualifier EmptyTags. Measured by the Kotlin adapter on okhttp and detekt-core: 432 stubs lose their facts (103 a receiver_type_hint, 11 a qualifier). Of 9 Kotlin edges a blind judge found right before the batch and unresolved after it, 5 are this (handshakeCertificates.sslSocketFactory() twice, EmptyTags.plus twice, compositeConfig.subConfig). It is the largest single cause of right edges lost by the Kotlin adapter. Not the same as the dedup that leaves a stub open beside its answer (a separate item): here the facts never reach a linker.\n\nEvidence and method: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/batch5a_11262026/ (DESIGN.md; php_RESULTS.md, java_RESULTS.md, kotlin_RESULTS.md; maps mine_e566 on the batch branch against before/ at dev 619ebe7ac; blind judgments judge/judgments_<lang>.jsonl scored by judge/score.py, samples seed 20261125). Found during batch 5a of ADR-0064 (java, kotlin, php)."  # 4409
